{
 "text": "Your setup page is already a procedure. Mark it up, and the build turns it into a skill an agent can follow, one step at a time.\n\nHere's the Example SDK's installation page. People read it as they always have: install the package, set your key, and check that it works.\n\nWrap the procedure in Agent Guide. Put each step in a Step component, with a Check that says how to tell it worked. Then add a Symptom for each error people hit.\n\nSome directions are for one reader. For Humans shows on the page, like where to find the button.\n\nFor Agents is hidden from people, and goes only to agents, like never ask for the key in the chat. It's hidden, not secret: anyone can read it in the page's source.\n\nBuild the site, and the guide compiles into a skill named after it. Steps come in order, each with its check, and the key step says Needs the user.\n\nNow an agent hits the module not found error. It reads the guide, searches, opens its troubleshooting, and answers with the fix and how to check it.\n\nStart with the agent guides page on the plugin's docs site.",
